Subject: [PATCH] fpcmoh: add FPC_IMG_DIAG tracing to the image message relayout

fpc_img_msg_relayout() silently returns whenever the blob's message state is
not the one it expects, which made a non-applied gap indistinguishable from a
gap that was applied too early or too late.

With FPC_IMG_DIAG=1 in the environment, log the state word, destination pointer,
received length and total at every call. Used while bringing up the a921; costs
nothing when the variable is unset.

---
libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c |   14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
@@ -188,7 +188,19 @@
 
   /* Not a message the blob is assembling into the image buffer. */
   if (state != 16 || *(guint8 **) (base + FPCBEP_OFF_DSTPTR) != msgbuf)
-    return;
+    {
+      if (self->relayout_img_msg && g_getenv ("FPC_IMG_DIAG"))
+        fp_warn ("IMG-DIAG: state %u dstptr %s msgbuf (recv_len %u total %u)",
+                 state,
+                 *(guint8 **) (base + FPCBEP_OFF_DSTPTR) == msgbuf ? "==" : "!=",
+                 recv_len, total);
+      return;
+    }
+
+  if (self->relayout_img_msg && g_getenv ("FPC_IMG_DIAG"))
+    fp_warn ("IMG-DIAG: state %u recv_len %u total %u want %u",
+             state, recv_len, total,
+             self->dev_ctx->img_w * self->dev_ctx->img_h);
 
   /* Nothing pending, or the message was already complete and dispatched inside
    * the call -- too late to help, and nothing here would be safe to touch. */
